```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9x9, fixed
  background: BLACK (0)
  input:
    content: 3-4 isolated GREY (5) pixels on BLACK background
    placement: each center at least 1 cell from every border (rows/cols 1-7)
    isolation: every center has full 3x3 BLACK neighborhood (only center is GREY)
    separation: Chebyshev distance >= 3 between any pair of centers (so 3x3 motifs never overlap)
  output:
    same 9x9 grid, all BLACK except 3x3 diamond motifs at each center
    motif: |
      5 1 5
      1 0 1
      5 1 5
    (GREY diagonals, BLUE orthogonals, BLACK center)
  transform: erase each GREY pixel, paint its 4 diagonal neighbors GREY and 4 orthogonal neighbors BLUE

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (constraints are simple enough for forward generation)
  steps:
    1. Create 9x9 BLACK grid
    2. Pick n = random(3, 4) center positions
    3. Place centers one at a time at random positions in rows/cols 1-7
    4. After each placement, reject if Chebyshev distance < 3 to any existing center
    5. Retry step 3-4 until n valid non-overlapping centers are placed (grid is sparse enough that acceptance rate is high)
    6. Set each center cell to GREY to form the input
```
