<description>
Stack all colored horizontal segments by increasing length, right-aligned above the solid bottom stripe.

Input structure
The grid has a dominant background, one full-width non-background stripe on
the bottom row, and one or more 4-connected monochrome foreground objects
above it. Each non-stripe object is a one-cell-thick horizontal segment.

Rule
Clear the segment objects from their original positions. Sort the segments
by length from shortest to longest, then place them in consecutive rows
immediately above the bottom stripe, with each segment right-aligned to the
grid's right edge. Keep the bottom stripe unchanged.

Key insight
The scattered segments are not moved by their original row or color; their
lengths define a stack order against the fixed bottom stripe.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "one-cell-thick monochrome horizontal segments above the full-width bottom stripe, ordered by increasing length",
  "dst": "consecutive right-aligned rows immediately above the bottom stripe, ordered top-to-bottom",
  "match_cond": "rank(s.length) == rank(d.row)",
  "transform": "clear each segment's old cells to background; preserve its color and length in the matched row; keep the bottom stripe unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: (n_segs+1)–(2*n_segs+1) rows x (n_segs+1) cols, where n_segs is 2–7
  background: 0
  stripe:
    description: full-width solid row of color 8 on the bottom row
  segments:
    count: exactly w-1 (one per length 1..w-1)
    lengths: exactly {1, 2, ..., w-1}, all unique
    each_segment: single-row horizontal contiguous bar, one cell thick
    colors: each segment has a distinct non-0 non-8 color; all colors unique
    placement: scattered above the stripe, each on its own row, at arbitrary horizontal position
    row_gaps: adjacent segment rows separated by 1–2 rows [observed]
    no segment on the row directly above the stripe [observed]
  output:
    all segments cleared from original positions
    segments stacked in consecutive rows immediately above the stripe
    sorted by length shortest(top) to longest(bottom), right-aligned to grid edge
    stripe unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick n_segs in [2,7], set w = n_segs + 1
    2. Pick h in [n_segs+1, 2*n_segs+1] (must have h-1 >= n_segs rows above stripe)
    3. Assign n_segs distinct colors from {1..9}\{8} to lengths 1..w-1
    4. Build output grid (h x w) with bg=0, stripe row h-1 all 8, segments right-aligned sorted by length in rows (h-1-n_segs) .. (h-2)
    5. To get input, clear the stacked segments and scatter each to a random row above the stripe (each on a unique row), at a random horizontal offset that fits within width
    6. Validate no two segments share a row and all rows are above the stripe
